      en: "The Sado Estuary, located immediately south of the Arrábida mountains near Setúbal, is a massive, highly biodiverse wetland system and one of the only places in Europe with a resident pod of bottlenose dolphins. The sheltered, nutrient-rich waters of the estuary provide an absolutely perfect environment for these magnificent marine mammals to hunt, breed, and thrive year-round. Beyond the famous dolphins, the estuary's sprawling salt marshes, mudflats, and sandbanks serve as a crucial habitat for thousands of wintering flamingos, storks, and other migratory wading birds." 
